<title>POLAND: Exbud pays PLN 8.0 mln for bridge builder.</title>
<headline>Exbud pays PLN 8.0 mln for bridge builder.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish construction firm Exbud SA paid 7.98 million zlotys for a 46.2-percent stake in a bridge construction firm  Kieleckie Przedsiebiorstwo Robot Mostowych SA (KPRM), the company said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>Exbud said it bought 600,000 shares in the firm,  which is the biggest bridge builder in Poland, but did not give other details.</p>
<p>Last year Exbud said it would further increase its stake in KPRM to a majority holding, after buying the 46.2-percent stake.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
